From d7464e16ee96814e4e9fc8059b3ea24b28588e3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:38:30 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Remove "make Chrome default browser" promos

This build is not a Chrome install and has no Play services, so asking
the user to make "Chrome" the default browser makes no sense. Every
promo surface is removed or switched off:

- First run: the DefaultBrowserPromoFirstRunFragment page is no longer
  added to the FRE page list (FirstRunActivity), even when the
  DefaultBrowserPromoFre flag is turned on. Welcome -> done is unchanged.
- App menu: the "Make Chrome default" item and its helpers are removed
  from TabbedAppMenuPropertiesDelegate.
- Settings: the "Default browser" row and the settings promo card
  (whose only provider is DefaultBrowserPromoCard) are removed from
  main_preferences.xml and MainSettings, including the settings-search
  hooks for them.
- Everything else goes through DefaultBrowserPromoUtils, which is made
  the single choke point: isFeatureEnabled() returns false (it used to
  depend on --disable-default-browser-promo) and now also gates
  shouldShowNonRoleManagerPromo() and shouldShowAppMenuItemEntryPoint().
  That covers the Role Manager dialog at startup
  (TabbedRootUiCoordinator) and from the Set-up list
  (ChromeTabbedActivity), the message banner after pasting a URL in the
  omnibox (LocationBarMediator.maybeShowDefaultBrowserPromo via
  AutocompleteMediator), and the Magic Stack educational-tip card.

Feature flags and strings are left untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
